# LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# note: Git for Windows checks out CRLF by default, which is invisible to whoever is running it.
# The libraries are still built, tested and packaged there, and a crate packaged from such a
# checkout carries CRLF onto the registry - a difference nobody would notice until it was
# published. It also breaks a test that reads source looking for `\n`, which is why `kamchatka`'s
# help test normalises what it reads as well.
* text=auto eol=lf
